 "source_status": "producer catalogue (Dossier Prethor 2020)",
 "units": "cm for H, a, widths and outline vertices (as printed); P in t/m (printed 'P(Tn/ml)')",
 "density_t_m3": 2.5,
 "density_note": "Prethor does not state a density; 2.5 t/m3 assumed. The VI and VA silhouettes, scaled with no fitting, reproduce every P within 0.7 % at 2.5 t/m3, which supports the assumption.",
 "published_note": "Nota: Los pesos son teóricos para las secciones indicadas. No incluyen recrecidos, peraltados, macizados ni repercusión de p.p. de cabezas.",
 "method": "Each family silhouette is an embedded raster image (PyMuPDF get_drawings finds only table cells, no vector outlines). Images were extracted at native resolution (0.46-1.03 cm/px), the grey-filled section masked, and scaled isotropically from the printed dimension lines; the drawn depth then matches one table size within about 1 % (the drawn size is recorded per family). Thicknesses were read from row/column runs with one stroke width (about 1 px) removed, then built into anchored parametric outlines: 'b' vertices fixed from the soffit, 't' vertices fixed from the top, 'ts' vertices fixed from the top and riding on the 1:4 outer web. Intersection-over-union of each outline against its traced mask at the drawn size is 0.95-0.985.",
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Printed per size: H and top width a (troughs) or top/bottom widths (VI); printed per family: bottom width (66, 80, 172, 198, 263, 330, 396, 300 cm). These are transcribed; everything else is scaled from the silhouettes (estimate).",
  "Outer webs of VA, VU, VC and the right web of VAA are 1:4 (a = b + H/2, or b + H/4 for VAA); this reproduces every printed a exactly except VUG (+1 cm printed, see family note).",
  "Only one silhouette per family is drawn (at the depth noted per family); other depths keep the flange/top/bottom details fixed and change web length only. The P tables are linear in H with a slope equal to the scaled web thickness, which supports this.",
  "Fillets drawn at flange/web junctions of VI and VA are modelled as the scaled sharp or chamfered corners; VAA-B's large bottom fillets are circular (R scaled).",
  "Vigas U and Vigas Cajón are drawn and modelled as open-topped troughs (no top slab), as are the VAA beams; the in-situ deck closes them. No interior ring is therefore present.",
  "VAA x origin: middle of the 3.00 m soffit; vertical outer web on the left (x = -1500 mm), 1:4 outer web on the right. Mirror for the opposite hand.",
  "The model's top width is exactly b + H/2 (b + H/4 for VAA); the printed a is that value rounded to 1 cm (e.g. VCP 80/220 H=95: 377.5 printed 3.78).",
  "Page 64 repeats page 63 (same image objects and table); page 63 is cited."
 ],
